  #h(36pt)The AICTE Activity Point Programme is an initiative that encourages students to participate in activities beyond regular classroom learning and gain practical exposure through community-based and socially relevant activities. The programme helps students connect their academic knowledge with real-world situations while developing essential skills such as communication, teamwork, problem-solving, leadership, technical awareness, and social responsibility.

  #h(36pt)As part of this programme, five activities were carried out in different areas including education, environmental awareness, and digital financial awareness. These activities provided opportunities to interact with students, local communities, businesses, and public places, thereby helping in understanding various social and practical aspects of everyday life.

  #h(36pt)The first activity focused on supporting rural students through a Summer Camp at Vivekananda College of Engineering and Technology (VCET), Puttur. Students were provided practical training in HTML, CSS, Canva, Office Tools, G-Suite, and SDGs, along with guidance on higher education, career opportunities, and future planning. They were also encouraged to participate in a hackathon, which helped develop their problem-solving, teamwork, communication, creativity, and digital skills.
  
  #h(36pt)The second activity was related to the Swachh Bharat Initiative and was conducted at Tannirbhavi Beach, Mangaluru, in association with the Department of Tourism, Mangalore. The activity involved active participation in maintaining cleanliness and creating awareness about environmental protection. Through beach cleaning and awareness activities, the importance of proper waste disposal, cleanliness of public spaces, and protection of coastal and marine environments was understood. The activity also developed a sense of civic responsibility, teamwork, and environmental awareness.

  #h(36pt)The third activity focused on facilitating 100% digitized money transactions and was carried out among local rickshaw drivers. Awareness was created regarding digital payment methods such as UPI, QR-code payments, mobile banking, and online transactions. Basic safety practices related to digital payments were also discussed. This activity helped in understanding the importance of digital literacy, financial inclusion, and secure cashless transactions in everyday life.

  #h(36pt)The fourth activity focused on managing and developing garbage disposal systems at a local residence in interior Vitla. The activity introduced the use of a biogas compost unit for sustainable waste management, renewable energy generation, and environmental protection. The fifth activity focused on tourism promotion and innovative approaches at Shri Anjaneya Temple, Bolwar, Puttur. The activity involved exploring and documenting a lesser-known heritage site and understanding how digital awareness can promote cultural and religious tourism.

  #h(36pt)These five activities provided meaningful practical exposure in different areas of society and helped in understanding the importance of education, cleanliness, digital technology, sustainable waste management, renewable energy, and cultural heritage. They also contributed to the development of communication, teamwork, problem-solving, social awareness, and responsible citizenship. Overall, the AICTE Activity Point Programme provided an opportunity to apply knowledge in real-life situations while contributing positively to the community and environment.

